dable and pretty much  any subject so here you can start using  memory master techniques I did a whole  video on this over on my video on  thinking like Sherlock Holmes I'll leave  the link in the description down below  recommend you check that out I'm going  to do more on memory in the future but  it's something I'd like to talk about  for now is using Anki flashcards so Anki  is a piece of software that helps you to  learn by looking at flashcards and then  testing your knowledge and it's supposed  to make you more likely to learn these  subjects that you're trying to learn  then competing software or competing  methods the reason for this is that it  applies to methods that have been  demonstrated in studies to be effective  the first is active recall basically  being asked questions being tested on  something is superior to just listening  to it and learning it in a passive way  this is why regurgitating and teaching  so useful it's why writing about it is  so useful but just remembering and  regurgitating out information back as we  did at school is also useful because  when we access information we're  practicing accessing it making it more  available and increasing those newer  connections at the same time Anke  flashcards use something called space -  learning space learning basically means  that you're asking yourself questions  you're rehearsing but then you're taking  a scheduled break at the optimum amount  of time and this has been shown in  studies to also increase our likelihood  of memorizing something the explanation  given for why this works is that it  allows the information to move from  short-term memory to long-term memory so  that we're then accessing it from there  again if you watched my video on working  memory and of course I recommend that  you do then you'll know that short-term  memory might not necessarily be a  storage container as people used to  think but rather it might just be  activation in our brain as in what seems  to be in a working memory is just the  neural connections that are activated or  that are potentiated it's when we  visualize something in our minds eye I  don't know what relation this would have  to space learning or why it works but I  suppose letting the neurons go cold and  then reactivating them might make them  more likely to form a long-term  connection but whatever I don't know why  this works but it does work and studies  demonstrate that it works and the other  great thing about Anki flashcards is  there's a huge community and you can  find stacks that other people have made  so if you want to learn about physiology  muscles of the leg a particular  programming language geography in a  particular area you'll be able to find  the flashcards that other people have  created online and download them and use  them for free so you can test yourself  wherever you are it's a really great  resource and it's a fantastic example of  using the Internet in order to learn  faster using not only the Internet as a  resource of information but using it as  a way to crowdsource all that  information and utilize the power of the  masses the groupthink there are many  more examples of accelerated learning  techniques many more tips you can  utilize in order to learn faster and for  longer however the main point of this  video other than the fact that you  should learn lots of different things is  that by combining the huge resource and  power of the internet with accelerated  learning techniques and with an end goal  in mind and then applying it to the gig  economy  our new economy we're staying in one job  for a long time isn't so common is an  incredibly powerful and worthwhile  endeavor I'd love to know what other  tips you have let me know in the  comments down below I'd love to know  what books you recommend what YouTube  channels all that let's discuss it  together thanks a ton for watching I  really appreciate it if you enjoyed this  video then please leave a like please  share it around that helps me out  immensely we're really close to 50,000  subscribers now which is awesome so  thanks a ton for that thanks also to  grant who's been doing a fantastic job  with the martial arts content and I've  got some more interesting contributors  hopefully lined up for you soon so stay  tuned there's lots of awesome stuff  coming to the channel very soon and in  the short term I'll be doing my promised  videos on Bruce Lee the myth vs. reality  as well as a real-life Bruce Wayne style  training program so if that sounds good  then subscribe I'll see you next time  thanks a ton for watching and bye for  now
 

